Package: dMod2
Type: Package
Title: Dynamic Modeling and Parameter Estimation in ODE Models
Version: 0.15.6
Date: 2026-11-05
Authors@R: c(
    person("Simon", "Beyer", email = "simon.beyer@fdm.uni-freiburg.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Daniel", "Kaschek", email = "daniel.kaschek@gmail.com", role = "aut",
           comment = "Created dMod 1.0; original design, philosophy"))
Description: Tools for dynamic modeling and parameter estimation in ordinary
    differential equation (ODE) models of reaction networks. Models are built
    symbolically and compiled to C/C++ with first- and second-order
    sensitivities. Prediction, observation and objective functions are
    composable function objects with their symbolic derivatives, following the
    paradigm that derivative information should be used for optimization
    whenever possible. Model calibration uses trust-region optimization with
    optional L1 penalties, multi-start search and profile-likelihood
    identifiability analysis, over experimental conditions that are integrated
    and evaluated in parallel. Mixed-effects models with normal, Laplace,
    spike-and-slab and Dirichlet-process random effects are fitted by
    expectation maximization with the Laplace approximation, sparse-grid
    quadrature or stochastic approximation. Measurements in relative units from
    separate experiments are aligned to common values, with the scaling factors
    of each experiment written as free expressions. Further tools cover steady states, solved symbolically or
    numerically within the parameter transformation, error models, and
    distributed computing on a cluster. Models, experimental
    conditions, measurements and parameter tables are imported from and
    exported to the 'PEtab' format, with 'SBML' import and export through
    'libSBML'.
